{"id": "swebq0237", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2404206890, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "where did russians originate?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0237.wav", "input_sha256": "d2754fccde65bb6b545dfa2e1c70c2b53d9919b0d3b957e71fc0562014755c1f", "input_samples": 28960, "input_s": 1.81, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.69, "act": 0.9977, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Russians originated primarily among the East Slavic peoples of Eastern Europe. More specifically, the Russian ethnos developed from East Slavic communities centered around Kievan Rus’ and later the northeastern Rus’ principalities, especially areas around Novgorod, Rostov-Suzdal, Vladimir, and Moscow. In short: Russians originated as East Slavs in the forest and steppe zones of Eastern Europe, especially in the lands of medieval Rus’.", "expert_answer": "Russians originated primarily among the **East Slavic peoples** of Eastern Europe.\n\nMore specifically, the Russian ethnos developed from East Slavic communities centered around **Kievan Rus’** and later the northeastern Rus’ principalities, especially areas around **Novgorod, Rostov-Suzdal, Vladimir, and Moscow**. Over time, these East Slavs mixed with neighboring **Finnic, Baltic, Turkic, and other peoples**, contributing to the formation of the Russian people.\n\nIn short: **Russians originated as East Slavs in the forest and steppe zones of Eastern Europe, especially in the lands of medieval Rus’.**", "transcript": "Where did Russians originate?\n", "asr_s": 0.62, "expert_s": 3.69, "expert_input_samples": 28960, "expert_input_s": 1.81, "exper